        "title": "policy: preview review-required gateway repairs",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Restack on current #99731 after #99720 merged and #99731 was cleaned up.\n- Add review-required `doctor --fix` previews for Gateway policy findings that should not be auto-mutated:\n  - `policy/gateway-non-loopback-bind`: previews setting `gateway.bind=loopback` for both `gateway.bind` and `gateway.customBindHost` non-loopback findings.\n  - `policy/gateway-node-command-denied`: previews appending the missing command to `gateway.nodes.denyCommands`.\n- Preserve skipped repair preview `changes` in the structured repair flow so review-required guidance is visible without counting the check as repaired.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nBehavior or issue addressed:\n`doctor --fix` now surfaces review-required preview guidance for Gateway bind and Gateway node-command policy findings without mutating config or counting the check as repaired.\n\nReal environment tested:\nWindows PowerShell in `C:\\src\\openclaw-policy-review-previews-push`, source checkout at PR head `40089645`, based on current #99731 head `c644a16a5d8ddfbd925943d5e8bc49e6738829f2`.\n\nExact steps or command run after this patch:\n1. `git diff --check HEAD~1..HEAD`\n2. `rg -n \"<<<<<<<|=======|>>>>>>>\" extensions/policy/src/doctor/register.test.ts extensions/policy/src/doctor/review-required-repairs.ts extensions/policy/src/doctor/scopes/gateway.ts src/flows/doctor-repair-flow.test.ts src/flows/doctor-repair-flow.ts`\n3. `git diff --stat origin/policy-doctor-gateway-http-repairs...HEAD`\n4. `git diff --name-status origin/policy-doctor-gateway-http-repairs...HEAD`\n\nEvidence after fix:\n`git diff --check HEAD~1..HEAD` exited 0. Conflict marker search returned no matches. The final PR diff is five files, 278 insertions and 3 deletions: `review-required-repairs.ts`, gateway scope repair hooks, policy doctor preview tests, and repair-flow skipped-preview propagation. The included tests cover non-loopback `gateway.bind`, non-loopback `gateway.customBindHost`, denied node-command previews, non-previewable findings without repair registration, and skipped repair preview `changes` surfacing through the repair flow.\n\nObserved result after fix:\nThe preview repair returns `status: skipped`, reason `policy repair requires review before changing config`, review warning/change text, and dry-run-safe config effects; it does not return a mutated config.\n\nWhat was not tested:\nThis clean push worktree has no `node_modules`, so I did not rerun Vitest locally after the restack. GitHub CI is running on the pushed PR head.\n\n## Stack\n\n- Stacked on #99731.\n- Keep draft until #99731 lands, then restack directly onto `main` and mark ready.",
